IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-definitions-products`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (1) -- Interpretation: ss 239, 239AA, 239A and 239B. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"`;
--   every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A term the Act borrows from another provision or another Act (entity, securities, debenture, business trust, corporation,
--   related corporation, voting shares, "prescribed" and "declared by the Authority") is a BOOLEAN fact named for what it states;
--   the seat layer works the keel's function out and passes the answer in, and never turns NOTHING into FALSE.

-- inert (reason 1), lines 37499-37509: Part 13, Division 1 and Subdivision (1) headings: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 37511-37511: s 239(1) chapeau "In this Division": introduces the definitions below, each encoded as its own function; creates no rule of its own.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 37720-37720: amendment marks.

§ `s 239(1): the defined terms of Part 13 Division 1`

-- "borrowing entity": an entity under a liability to repay money received in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase its debentures.
-- src:37513 | “borrowing entity” means an entity that is or will be under a
-- src:37514 | liability (whether or not such liability is present or future) to
-- src:37515 | repay any money received by it in response to an invitation to
-- src:37516 | subscribe for or purchase debentures of the entity;
@ref s 239(1) "borrowing entity" (src:37513-37516)
GIVEN
    `the body is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
    `the entity is or will be under a liability to repay money it received in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity, or will it be, under a liability (present or future) to repay money it received in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase its debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "borrowing entity" the body is a borrowing entity` MEANS
    IF `the body is an entity` AND `the entity is or will be under a liability to repay money it received in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an entity that is or will be under a liability (whether or not such liability is present or future) to repay any money received by it in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the entity"

-- "control": the capacity to determine the outcome of decisions on the financial and operating policies of the entity, having regard to (a) and (b); the exclusion is for influence the law, a contract or a court order requires to be used for others.
-- src:37518 | “control”, in relation to an entity, means the capacity of a person
-- src:37519 | to determine the outcome of decisions on the financial and
-- src:37520 | operating policies of the entity, having regard to —
-- src:37522 | (a) the influence which the person can, in practice, exert
-- src:37523 | on the entity (as opposed to the rights which the
-- src:37524 | person can exercise in the entity); and
-- src:37526 | (b) any practice or pattern of behaviour of the person
-- src:37527 | affecting the financial or operating policies of the
-- src:37528 | entity (even if such practice or pattern of behaviour
-- src:37529 | involves a breach of an agreement or a breach of
-- src:37530 | trust),
-- src:37532 | but does not include any capacity of a person to influence
-- src:37533 | decisions on the financial and operating policies of the entity
-- src:37534 | if such influence is required by law or under any contract or
-- src:37535 | order of court to be exercised for the benefit of other persons;
@ref s 239(1) "control" (src:37518-37535)
GIVEN
    `the person has the capacity to determine the outcome of decisions on the financial and operating policies of the entity, having regard to the influence the person can in practice exert on the entity and to any practice or pattern of behaviour of the person affecting those policies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to the influence the person can in practice exert on the entity (as opposed to the rights the person can exercise in it) and to any practice or pattern of behaviour of the person affecting its financial or operating policies (even one that involves a breach of an agreement or of trust), can the person determine the outcome of decisions on the entity's financial and operating policies?
    `the capacity is only a capacity to influence decisions on those policies, and such influence is required by law or under a contract or order of court to be exercised for the benefit of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the capacity only a capacity to influence decisions on the entity's financial and operating policies, where the law, a contract or an order of court requires that influence to be exercised for the benefit of other persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "control" the person has control of the entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the capacity is only a capacity to influence decisions on those policies, and such influence is required by law or under a contract or order of court to be exercised for the benefit of other persons`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any capacity of a person to influence decisions on the financial and operating policies of the entity if such influence is required by law or under any contract or order of court to be exercised for the benefit of other persons"
        IF `the person has the capacity to determine the outcome of decisions on the financial and operating policies of the entity, having regard to the influence the person can in practice exert on the entity and to any practice or pattern of behaviour of the person affecting those policies`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the capacity of a person to determine the outcome of decisions on the financial and operating policies of the entity"

-- "dealing in capital markets products", for securities and securities-based derivatives contracts, as this Division uses it.
-- src:37540 | “dealing in capital markets products”, in respect of capital
-- src:37541 | markets products that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:37542 | derivatives contracts, means (whether as principal or
-- src:37543 | agent) —
-- src:37545 | (a) making or offering to make with any person; or
-- src:37547 | (b) inducing or attempting to induce any person to enter
-- src:37548 | into or to offer to enter into,
-- src:37550 | any agreement for or with a view to acquiring, disposing of,
-- src:37551 | subscribing for, entering into, effecting, arranging or
-- src:37552 | underwriting any securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:37553 | contracts;
@ref s 239(1) "dealing in capital markets products" (src:37540-37553)
GIVEN
    `the capital markets products are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the capital markets products securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person makes or offers to make an agreement with any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person, as principal or agent, make or offer to make an agreement with any person?
    `the person induces or attempts to induce any person to enter into or to offer to enter into an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person, as principal or agent, induce or attempt to induce any person to enter into, or to offer to enter into, an agreement?
    `the agreement is for or with a view to acquiring, disposing of, subscribing for, entering into, effecting, arranging or underwriting securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement for, or with a view to, acquiring, disposing of, subscribing for, entering into, effecting, arranging or underwriting any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "dealing in capital markets products" the activity is dealing in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` MEANS
    IF `the capital markets products are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` AND (`the person makes or offers to make an agreement with any person` OR `the person induces or attempts to induce any person to enter into or to offer to enter into an agreement`) AND `the agreement is for or with a view to acquiring, disposing of, subscribing for, entering into, effecting, arranging or underwriting securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, means (whether as principal or agent) (a) making or offering to make with any person; or (b) inducing or attempting to induce any person to enter into or to offer to enter into, any agreement for or with a view to acquiring, disposing of, subscribing for, entering into, effecting, arranging or underwriting any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

-- "debenture issuance programme".
-- src:37555 | “debenture issuance programme” means any scheme or
-- src:37556 | arrangement by an entity for the issue of debentures or
-- src:37557 | units of debentures where only part of the maximum amount
-- src:37558 | or aggregate number of debentures or units of debentures
-- src:37559 | under the programme is offered initially and a further tranche
-- src:37560 | or tranches may be offered subsequently;
@ref s 239(1) "debenture issuance programme" (src:37555-37560)
GIVEN
    `the scheme or arrangement is by an entity for the issue of debentures or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme or arrangement one by an entity for the issue of debentures or units of debentures?
    `only part of the maximum amount or aggregate number of debentures or units of debentures under the programme is offered initially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is only part of the maximum amount (or aggregate number) of debentures or units of debentures under the programme offered initially?
    `a further tranche or tranches may be offered subsequently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May a further tranche or tranches be offered later?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "debenture issuance programme" the arrangement is a debenture issuance programme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme or arrangement is by an entity for the issue of debentures or units of debentures` AND `only part of the maximum amount or aggregate number of debentures or units of debentures under the programme is offered initially` AND `a further tranche or tranches may be offered subsequently`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any scheme or arrangement by an entity for the issue of debentures or units of debentures where only part of the maximum amount or aggregate number of debentures or units of debentures under the programme is offered initially and a further tranche or tranches may be offered subsequently"

-- "expert": handed to section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 (another Act, not a source here: the fact is asked).
-- src:37562 | “expert” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the
-- src:37563 | Companies Act 1967;
@ref s 239(1) "expert" (src:37562-37563)
GIVEN
    `the person is an expert within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an expert as section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 defines "expert"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "expert" the person is an expert` MEANS
    IF `the person is an expert within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967"

-- "guarantor entity".
-- src:37565 | “guarantor entity”, in relation to a borrowing entity, means an
-- src:37566 | entity that has guaranteed or has agreed to guarantee the
-- src:37567 | repayment of any money received or to be received by the
-- src:37568 | borrowing entity in response to an invitation to subscribe for
-- src:37569 | or purchase debentures of the borrowing entity;
@ref s 239(1) "guarantor entity" (src:37565-37569)
GIVEN
    `the body is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
    `the entity has guaranteed or has agreed to guarantee the repayment of money received or to be received by the borrowing entity in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase its debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity guaranteed, or agreed to guarantee, the repayment of money the borrowing entity has received or is to receive in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase the borrowing entity's debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "guarantor entity" the body is a guarantor entity of the borrowing entity` MEANS
    IF `the body is an entity` AND `the entity has guaranteed or has agreed to guarantee the repayment of money received or to be received by the borrowing entity in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase its debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a borrowing entity, means an entity that has guaranteed or has agreed to guarantee the repayment of any money received or to be received by the borrowing entity in response to an invitation to subscribe for or purchase debentures of the borrowing entity"

-- "immediate family": a closed list, over the core's `Family relation`.
-- src:37571 | “immediate family”, in relation to an individual, means the
-- src:37572 | individual’s spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter,
-- src:37573 | adopted daughter, stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother,
-- src:37574 | stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister or stepsister;
@ref s 239(1) "immediate family" (src:37571-37574)
GIVEN
    `the relation of the person to the individual` IS A `Family relation` @desc What is the person's relation to the individual: a spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter, stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother, stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister, stepsister, or some other relation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "immediate family" the person is in the immediate family of the individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relation of the person to the individual`
    WHEN `some other relation` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the individual's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter, stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother, stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister or stepsister"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "issuer": one meaning for each kind of offer.
DECLARE `s 239(1) "issuer" kind of offer` IS ONE OF
    `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust`
    `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of units in a business trust`
    `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust`
    `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of something else`

-- src:37576 | “issuer” means —
-- src:37578 | (a) in relation to an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:37579 | derivatives contracts (other than units or derivatives
-- src:37580 | of units in a business trust), the entity that issues or
-- src:37581 | will be issuing the securities or securities‑based
-- src:37582 | derivatives contracts being offered;
-- src:37587 | (b) in relation to an offer of units in a business trust, the
-- src:37588 | trustee‑manager of the business trust in its capacity as
-- src:37589 | the trustee that issues or will be issuing the units; and
-- src:37591 | (c) in relation to an offer of derivatives of units in a
-- src:37592 | business trust, the trustee‑manager of the business
-- src:37593 | trust in its capacity as the trustee, or any other entity
-- src:37594 | that issues or will be issuing the derivatives of units;
@ref s 239(1) "issuer" (src:37576-37594)
GIVEN
    `the kind of offer` IS A `s 239(1) "issuer" kind of offer` @desc What is offered: securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust, units in a business trust, derivatives of units in a business trust, or something else?
    `the person is the entity that issues or will be issuing the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the entity that issues, or will be issuing, the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered?
    `the person is the trustee-manager of the business trust, in its capacity as the trustee that issues or will be issuing the units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee-manager of the business trust, acting in its capacity as the trustee that issues, or will be issuing, the units?
    `the person is the trustee-manager of the business trust, in its capacity as the trustee that issues or will be issuing the derivatives of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee-manager of the business trust, acting in its capacity as the trustee that issues, or will be issuing, the derivatives of units?
    `the person is any other entity that issues or will be issuing the derivatives of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person any other entity that issues, or will be issuing, the derivatives of units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "issuer" the person is the issuer in relation to the offer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of offer`
    WHEN `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust` THEN
        IF `the person is the entity that issues or will be issuing the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust), the entity that issues or will be issuing the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered"
    WHEN `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of units in a business trust` THEN
        IF `the person is the trustee-manager of the business trust, in its capacity as the trustee that issues or will be issuing the units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an offer of units in a business trust, the trustee-manager of the business trust in its capacity as the trustee that issues or will be issuing the units"
    WHEN `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust` THEN
        IF `the person is the trustee-manager of the business trust, in its capacity as the trustee that issues or will be issuing the derivatives of units` OR `the person is any other entity that issues or will be issuing the derivatives of units`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust, the trustee-manager of the business trust in its capacity as the trustee, or any other entity that issues or will be issuing the derivatives of units"
    WHEN `s 239(1) "issuer" an offer of something else` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the three limbs speak only of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts

-- "minimum subscription": the amount a prospectus states as the minimum that must be raised, failing which nothing is allotted.
-- src:37596 | “minimum subscription”, in relation to any securities or
-- src:37597 | securities‑based derivatives contracts offered for
-- src:37598 | subscription, means the amount stated in the prospectus
-- src:37599 | relating to the offer as the minimum amount which must be
-- src:37600 | raised by the issue of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:37601 | derivatives contracts so offered, failing which no securities or
-- src:37602 | securities‑based derivatives contracts will be allotted or
-- src:37603 | issued;
@ref s 239(1) "minimum subscription" (src:37596-37603)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus states an amount as the minimum amount which must be raised by the issue of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus for the offer state an amount as the minimum amount which must be raised by the issue of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered?
    `the prospectus says that if that amount is not raised no securities or securities-based derivatives contracts will be allotted or issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus say that, if that amount is not raised, no securities or securities-based derivatives contracts will be allotted or issued?
    `the amount the prospectus states as the minimum amount, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the prospectus state as the minimum amount that must be raised, in Singapore dollars (0 if it states none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 239(1) "minimum subscription" the amount of the minimum subscription` MEANS
    IF `the prospectus states an amount as the minimum amount which must be raised by the issue of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered` AND `the prospectus says that if that amount is not raised no securities or securities-based derivatives contracts will be allotted or issued`
    THEN JUST `the amount the prospectus states as the minimum amount, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the definition names the amount a prospectus states, so a prospectus that states none has no minimum subscription to report

-- "preliminary document".
-- src:37605 | “preliminary document” means a document which has been
-- src:37606 | lodged with the Authority and is issued for the purpose of
-- src:37607 | determining the appropriate issue or sale price of, and the
-- src:37608 | number of, securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:37609 | to be issued or sold and which contains the information
-- src:37610 | required to be included in a prospectus under section 243,
-- src:37611 | except for such information as the Authority may prescribe;
@ref s 239(1) "preliminary document" (src:37605-37611)
GIVEN
    `the document has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the document been lodged with the Authority?
    `the document is issued for the purpose of determining the appropriate issue or sale price of, and the number of, securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to be issued or sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document issued for the purpose of determining the appropriate issue or sale price of, and the number of, the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to be issued or sold?
    `the document contains the information required to be included in a prospectus under section 243, except for such information as the Authority may prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document contain the information section 243 requires in a prospectus, apart from any information the Authority has prescribed may be left out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "preliminary document" the document is a preliminary document` MEANS
    IF `the document has been lodged with the Authority` AND `the document is issued for the purpose of determining the appropriate issue or sale price of, and the number of, securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to be issued or sold` AND `the document contains the information required to be included in a prospectus under section 243, except for such information as the Authority may prescribe`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a document which has been lodged with the Authority and is issued for the purpose of determining the appropriate issue or sale price of, and the number of, securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to be issued or sold and which contains the information required to be included in a prospectus under section 243, except for such information as the Authority may prescribe"

-- "product highlights sheet" and "profile statement": pointers into ss 240AA(1) and 240(4), which are encoded in sfac-240.l4.
-- src:37613 | “product highlights sheet” means a product highlights sheet
-- src:37614 | referred to in section 240AA(1);
@ref s 239(1) "product highlights sheet" (src:37613-37614)
GIVEN
    `the document is a product highlights sheet referred to in section 240AA(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a product highlights sheet of the kind section 240AA(1) refers to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "product highlights sheet" the document is a product highlights sheet` MEANS
    IF `the document is a product highlights sheet referred to in section 240AA(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a product highlights sheet referred to in section 240AA(1)"

-- src:37616 | “profile statement” means a profile statement referred to in
-- src:37617 | section 240(4);
@ref s 239(1) "profile statement" (src:37616-37617)
GIVEN
    `the document is a profile statement referred to in section 240(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a profile statement of the kind section 240(4) refers to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "profile statement" the document is a profile statement` MEANS
    IF `the document is a profile statement referred to in section 240(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a profile statement referred to in section 240(4)"

-- "promoter".
-- src:37619 | “promoter”, in relation to a prospectus issued by or in
-- src:37620 | connection with an entity or a business trust, means a
-- src:37621 | promoter of the entity or business trust (as the case may be)
-- src:37622 | who was a party to the preparation of the prospectus or of any
-- src:37623 | relevant portion thereof, but does not include any person by
-- src:37624 | reason only of the person acting in a professional capacity;
@ref s 239(1) "promoter" (src:37619-37624)
GIVEN
    `the person is a promoter of the entity or business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a promoter of the entity or business trust the prospectus is issued by or in connection with?
    `the person was a party to the preparation of the prospectus or of a relevant portion of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person a party to the preparation of the prospectus, or of any relevant portion of it?
    `the person is within the term only by reason of acting in a professional capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person count as a promoter only by reason of acting in a professional capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "promoter" the person is a promoter in relation to the prospectus` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is within the term only by reason of acting in a professional capacity`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any person by reason only of the person acting in a professional capacity"
        IF `the person is a promoter of the entity or business trust` AND `the person was a party to the preparation of the prospectus or of a relevant portion of it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a promoter of the entity or business trust (as the case may be) who was a party to the preparation of the prospectus or of any relevant portion thereof"

-- "prospectus": the exclusions are tested first.
-- src:37626 | “prospectus” means any prospectus, notice, circular, material,
-- src:37627 | advertisement, publication or other document used to make
-- src:37628 | an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:37633 | contracts, and includes any document deemed to be a
-- src:37634 | prospectus under section 257, but does not include —
-- src:37636 | (a) a profile statement;
-- src:37638 | (b) any material, advertisement or publication which is
-- src:37639 | authorised by section 251 (other than subsection (5));
-- src:37640 | or
-- src:37642 | (c) a product highlights sheet;
@ref s 239(1) "prospectus" (src:37626-37642)
GIVEN
    `the document is a prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document used to make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document used to make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the document is deemed to be a prospectus under section 257` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document deemed to be a prospectus under section 257?
    `the document is a profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a profile statement?
    `the document is material, an advertisement or a publication authorised by section 251, other than by section 251(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document material, an advertisement or a publication that section 251 authorises (other than under section 251(5))?
    `the document is a product highlights sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a product highlights sheet?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "prospectus" the document is a prospectus` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the document is a profile statement` OR `the document is material, an advertisement or a publication authorised by section 251, other than by section 251(5)` OR `the document is a product highlights sheet`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (a) a profile statement; (b) any material, advertisement or publication which is authorised by section 251 (other than subsection (5)); or (c) a product highlights sheet"
        IF `the document is a prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document used to make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` OR `the document is deemed to be a prospectus under section 257`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any prospectus, notice, circular, material, advertisement, publication or other document used to make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, and includes any document deemed to be a prospectus under section 257"

-- "recognised securities exchange".
-- src:37644 | “recognised securities exchange” means a corporation which
-- src:37645 | has been declared by the Authority, by order in the Gazette, to
-- src:37646 | be a recognised securities exchange for the purposes of this
-- src:37647 | Division;
@ref s 239(1) "recognised securities exchange" (src:37644-37647)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the Authority has declared by order in the Gazette that the corporation is a recognised securities exchange for the purposes of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by order in the Gazette, declared the corporation to be a recognised securities exchange for the purposes of this Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "recognised securities exchange" the corporation is a recognised securities exchange` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation` AND `the Authority has declared by order in the Gazette that the corporation is a recognised securities exchange for the purposes of this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a corporation which has been declared by the Authority, by order in the Gazette, to be a recognised securities exchange for the purposes of this Division"

-- "related party", (a) in relation to an entity.
-- src:37649 | “related party” means —
-- src:37651 | (a) in relation to an entity —
-- src:37653 | (i) a director or an equivalent person of the entity;
-- src:37655 | (ii) the chief executive officer or equivalent person
-- src:37656 | of the entity;
-- src:37658 | (iii) a person who controls the entity;
-- src:37660 | (iv) a related corporation;
-- src:37662 | (v) any other entity controlled by it;
-- src:37664 | (vi) any other entity controlled by the person
-- src:37665 | referred to in sub‑paragraph (iii); and
-- src:37667 | (vii) a related party of any individual referred to in
-- src:37668 | sub‑paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii); and
@ref s 239(1) "related party" (a) (src:37649-37668)
GIVEN
    `the person is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director, or an equivalent person, of the entity?
    `the person is the chief executive officer or an equivalent person of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the chief executive officer, or an equivalent person, of the entity?
    `the person controls the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person control the entity (as section 239(1) defines "control")?
    `the person is a related corporation of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a related corporation of the entity (as section 2(1) defines "related corporation")?
    `the person is another entity controlled by the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person another entity that the entity controls?
    `the person is another entity controlled by a person who controls the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person another entity that is controlled by a person who controls the entity?
    `the person is a related party, in relation to an individual, of an individual who is a director, chief executive officer or controller of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a related party (as paragraph (b) of the definition, in relation to an individual) of an individual who is a director or equivalent person, the chief executive officer or equivalent person, or a person who controls the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "related party" (a) the person is a related party of the entity` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` OR `the person is the chief executive officer or an equivalent person of the entity` OR `the person controls the entity` OR `the person is a related corporation of the entity` OR `the person is another entity controlled by the entity` OR `the person is another entity controlled by a person who controls the entity` OR `the person is a related party, in relation to an individual, of an individual who is a director, chief executive officer or controller of the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) in relation to an entity (i) a director or an equivalent person of the entity; (ii) the chief executive officer or equivalent person of the entity; (iii) a person who controls the entity; (iv) a related corporation; (v) any other entity controlled by it; (vi) any other entity controlled by the person referred to in sub-paragraph (iii); and (vii) a related party of any individual referred to in sub-paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii)"

-- "related party", (b) in relation to an individual. The 30% is asked as votes, so the boundary is exact.
-- src:37670 | (b) in relation to an individual —
-- src:37672 | (i) his or her immediate family;
-- src:37674 | (ii) a trustee of any trust of which the individual or
-- src:37675 | any member of the individual’s immediate
-- src:37676 | family is —
-- src:37678 | (A) a beneficiary; or
-- src:37680 | (B) where the trust is a discretionary trust, a
-- src:37681 | discretionary object,
-- src:37686 | (ii) when the trustee acts in that capacity; and
-- src:37688 | (iii) any corporation in which the individual and his
-- src:37689 | or her immediate family (whether directly or
-- src:37690 | indirectly) have interests in voting shares of an
-- src:37691 | aggregate of not less than 30% of the total votes
-- src:37692 | attached to all voting shares;
@ref s 239(1) "related party" (b) (src:37670-37692)
GIVEN
    `the person is in the immediate family of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the individual's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter, stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother, stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister or stepsister?
    `the person is a trustee of a trust of which the individual or a member of the individual's immediate family is a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee of a trust of which the individual, or a member of the individual's immediate family, is a beneficiary?
    `the person is a trustee of a discretionary trust of which the individual or a member of the individual's immediate family is a discretionary object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee of a discretionary trust of which the individual, or a member of the individual's immediate family, is a discretionary object?
    `the trustee is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee acting in that capacity (as trustee of that trust)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation in which the individual and the individual's immediate family have interests, directly or indirectly` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are attached to the voting shares in the corporation in which the individual and the individual's immediate family together have interests, directly or indirectly?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of votes attached to all the voting shares in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "related party" (b) the person is a related party of the individual` MEANS
    IF `the person is in the immediate family of the individual` OR ((`the person is a trustee of a trust of which the individual or a member of the individual's immediate family is a beneficiary` OR `the person is a trustee of a discretionary trust of which the individual or a member of the individual's immediate family is a discretionary object`) AND `the trustee is acting in that capacity`) OR (`the person is a corporation` AND (`the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the corporation` GREATER THAN 0) AND ((`the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation in which the individual and the individual's immediate family have interests, directly or indirectly` DIVIDED BY `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the corporation`) AT LEAST 30%))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to an individual (i) his or her immediate family; (ii) a trustee of any trust of which the individual or any member of the individual's immediate family is (A) a beneficiary; or (B) where the trust is a discretionary trust, a discretionary object ... when the trustee acts in that capacity; and (iii) any corporation in which the individual and his or her immediate family (whether directly or indirectly) have interests in voting shares of an aggregate of not less than 30% of the total votes attached to all voting shares"

-- "replacement document", "supplementary document", "statutory meeting", "trust deed", "trust property": pointers and borrowed meanings.
