@ref s 239(1) "trust property" (src:37708-37709)
GIVEN
    `the property is trust property within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property "trust property" as section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004 defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "trust property" the property is trust property` MEANS
    IF `the property is trust property within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004"

-- "underlying entity" and "unit" (of a share or debenture).
-- src:37711 | “underlying entity”, in relation to an offer of units of shares or
-- src:37712 | debentures, means the entity the shares or debentures of
-- src:37713 | which are the subject of the offer;
@ref s 239(1) "underlying entity" (src:37711-37713)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of units of shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units of shares or of debentures?
    `the body is the entity the shares or debentures of which are the subject of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the entity whose shares or debentures are the subject of the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "underlying entity" the body is the underlying entity of the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of units of shares or debentures` AND `the body is the entity the shares or debentures of which are the subject of the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an offer of units of shares or debentures, means the entity the shares or debentures of which are the subject of the offer"

-- src:37715 | “unit”, in relation to a share or debenture, means any right or
-- src:37716 | interest, whether legal or equitable, in the share or debenture,
-- src:37717 | by whatever name called, and includes any option to acquire
-- src:37718 | any such right or interest in the share or debenture.
@ref s 239(1) "unit" (of a share or debenture) (src:37715-37718)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the share or debenture, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a right or interest, legal or equitable and by whatever name called, in the share or debenture?
    `the thing is an option to acquire such a right or interest in the share or debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an option to acquire such a right or interest in the share or debenture?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(1) "unit" the thing is a unit of a share or debenture` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the share or debenture, by whatever name called` OR `the thing is an option to acquire such a right or interest in the share or debenture`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a share or debenture, means any right or interest, whether legal or equitable, in the share or debenture, by whatever name called, and includes any option to acquire any such right or interest in the share or debenture"

§ `s 239(2) to (8): deemed inclusions, deemed debentures, the Authority's notices, and what an offer is`

-- s 239(2): a statement in a report or memorandum is deemed included in the prospectus or profile statement.
-- src:37722 | (2) For the purposes of this Division, a statement is deemed to be
-- src:37723 | included in a prospectus or profile statement if it is contained in any
-- src:37724 | report or memorandum appearing on the face thereof or by reference
-- src:37725 | incorporated therein or issued therewith.
@ref s 239(2) (src:37722-37725)
GIVEN
    `the statement is contained in a report or memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement contained in a report or memorandum?
    `the report or memorandum appears on the face of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report or memorandum appear on the face of the prospectus or profile statement?
    `the report or memorandum is incorporated in the prospectus or profile statement by reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report or memorandum incorporated in the prospectus or profile statement by reference?
    `the report or memorandum is issued with the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report or memorandum issued with the prospectus or profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(2) the statement is deemed to be included in the prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement is contained in a report or memorandum` AND (`the report or memorandum appears on the face of the prospectus or profile statement` OR `the report or memorandum is incorporated in the prospectus or profile statement by reference` OR `the report or memorandum is issued with the prospectus or profile statement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement is deemed to be included in a prospectus or profile statement if it is contained in any report or memorandum appearing on the face thereof or by reference incorporated therein or issued therewith"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 239(3): an invitation to deposit or lend is deemed an offer of debentures, and the acknowledgment document is deemed a debenture.
-- src:37727 | (3) For the purposes of this Division —
-- src:37729 | (a) any invitation to a person to deposit money with or to lend
-- src:37730 | money to an entity is deemed to be an offer of debentures
-- src:37731 | of the entity; and
@ref s 239(3)(a) (src:37727-37731)
GIVEN
    `the invitation is an invitation to a person to deposit money with or to lend money to an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the invitation one to a person to deposit money with, or to lend money to, an entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(3)(a) the invitation is deemed to be an offer of debentures of the entity` MEANS
    IF `the invitation is an invitation to a person to deposit money with or to lend money to an entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming reaches "any invitation to a person to deposit money with or to lend money to an entity" and says nothing of an invitation of any other kind

-- src:37736 | (b) any document that is issued or intended or required to be
-- src:37737 | issued by an entity acknowledging or evidencing or
-- src:37738 | constituting an acknowledgment of the indebtedness of
-- src:37739 | the entity in respect of any money that is or may be
-- src:37740 | deposited with or lent to the entity in response to such an
-- src:37741 | invitation is deemed to be a debenture.
@ref s 239(3)(b) (src:37736-37741)
GIVEN
    `the document is issued or intended or required to be issued by an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document issued, or intended or required to be issued, by an entity?
    `the document acknowledges, evidences or constitutes an acknowledgment of the entity's indebtedness for money deposited with or lent to the entity in response to such an invitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document acknowledge, evidence or constitute an acknowledgment of the entity's indebtedness for money deposited with or lent to the entity in response to an invitation to deposit or lend?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(3)(b) the document is deemed to be a debenture` MEANS
    IF `the document is issued or intended or required to be issued by an entity` AND `the document acknowledges, evidences or constitutes an acknowledgment of the entity's indebtedness for money deposited with or lent to the entity in response to such an invitation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming reaches the document described and says nothing of any other document

-- s 239(4): "prescribed entity" and "deposit" (for ss 239(3A) and 239(5)).
-- src:37759 | (4) In subsections (3A) and (5) —
-- src:37761 | “deposit” has the meaning given by section 4B(4) of the
-- src:37762 | Banking Act 1970;
@ref s 239(4) "deposit" (src:37759-37762)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a deposit within section 4B(4) of the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a deposit as section 4B(4) of the Banking Act 1970 defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(4) "deposit" the thing is a deposit` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a deposit within section 4B(4) of the Banking Act 1970`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 4B(4) of the Banking Act 1970"

-- src:37764 | “prescribed entity” means —
-- src:37766 | (a) any bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or
-- src:37768 | (b) any entity or any entity of a class which has been
-- src:37769 | declared by the Authority, by order in the Gazette, to
-- src:37770 | be a prescribed entity for the purposes of this
-- src:37771 | subsection.
@ref s 239(4) "prescribed entity" (src:37764-37771)
GIVEN
    `the body is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the Authority has declared by order in the Gazette that the entity, or an entity of its class, is a prescribed entity for the purposes of section 239(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by order in the Gazette, declared the entity (or its class of entity) to be a prescribed entity for the purposes of section 239(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(4) "prescribed entity" the body is a prescribed entity` MEANS
    IF `the body is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` OR `the Authority has declared by order in the Gazette that the entity, or an entity of its class, is a prescribed entity for the purposes of section 239(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) any bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or (b) any entity or any entity of a class which has been declared by the Authority, by order in the Gazette, to be a prescribed entity for the purposes of this subsection"

-- s 239(3A): despite subsection (3), a prescribed entity's invitation to make a deposit is not an offer of debentures, and its certificates of deposit and deposit acknowledgments are not debentures.
-- src:37743 | (3A) Despite subsection (3) —
-- src:37745 | (a) any invitation to a person by a prescribed entity to make a
-- src:37746 | deposit with the prescribed entity is not an offer of
-- src:37747 | debentures; and
@ref s 239(3A)(a) (src:37743-37747)
GIVEN
    `the body is a prescribed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a prescribed entity as section 239(4) defines it?
    `the invitation is an invitation to a person to make a deposit with the prescribed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the invitation one to a person to make a deposit with the prescribed entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(3A)(a) the invitation by the prescribed entity is an offer of debentures` MEANS
    IF `the body is a prescribed entity` AND `the invitation is an invitation to a person to make a deposit with the prescribed entity`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any invitation to a person by a prescribed entity to make a deposit with the prescribed entity is not an offer of debentures"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3A)(a) says no only of an invitation by a prescribed entity to make a deposit with it

-- src:37749 | (b) the following documents issued or intended or required to
-- src:37750 | be issued by a prescribed entity are not debentures:
-- src:37752 | (i) any certificate of deposit;
-- src:37754 | (ii) any other document acknowledging or evidencing or
-- src:37755 | constituting an acknowledgment of the indebtedness
-- src:37756 | of the prescribed entity in respect of any deposit that
-- src:37757 | is or may be made with the prescribed entity.
@ref s 239(3A)(b) (src:37749-37757)
GIVEN
    `the body is a prescribed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a prescribed entity as section 239(4) defines it?
    `the document is issued or intended or required to be issued by the prescribed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document issued, or intended or required to be issued, by the prescribed entity?
    `the document is a certificate of deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a certificate of deposit?
    `the document acknowledges, evidences or constitutes an acknowledgment of the prescribed entity's indebtedness for a deposit that is or may be made with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document acknowledge, evidence or constitute an acknowledgment of the prescribed entity's indebtedness for a deposit that is or may be made with it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(3A)(b) the document issued by the prescribed entity is a debenture` MEANS
    IF `the body is a prescribed entity` AND `the document is issued or intended or required to be issued by the prescribed entity` AND (`the document is a certificate of deposit` OR `the document acknowledges, evidences or constitutes an acknowledgment of the prescribed entity's indebtedness for a deposit that is or may be made with it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following documents issued or intended or required to be issued by a prescribed entity are not debentures"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3A)(b) says no only of the two kinds of document it lists

-- s 239(3) and (3A) read together, for the person who asks whether an invitation to deposit or lend is an offer of debentures.
-- src:37743 | (3A) Despite subsection (3) —
-- src:37745 | (a) any invitation to a person by a prescribed entity to make a
-- src:37746 | deposit with the prescribed entity is not an offer of
-- src:37747 | debentures; and
@ref s 239(3A)(a) read with section 239(3)(a) (src:37743-37747)
GIVEN
    `what section 239(3)(a) answers for the invitation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239(3)(a) the invitation is deemed to be an offer of debentures of the entity` answer for the invitation? (NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 239(3A)(a) answers for the invitation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239(3A)(a) the invitation by the prescribed entity is an offer of debentures` answer for the invitation? (NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(3) and (3A) the invitation to deposit or lend is an offer of debentures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `what section 239(3A)(a) answers for the invitation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite subsection (3) (a) any invitation to a person by a prescribed entity to make a deposit with the prescribed entity is not an offer of debentures"
        IF `what section 239(3)(a) answers for the invitation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither subsection (3)(a) nor subsection (3A)(a) reaches the invitation

-- s 239(4A): a reference to a debenture includes one issued by a trustee on behalf of a trust.
-- src:37773 | (4A) For the purposes of this Division, references to a debenture
-- src:37774 | includes a debenture, or a unit of debenture, issued by a trustee of a
-- src:37775 | trust on behalf of the trust.
@ref s 239(4A) (src:37773-37775)
GIVEN
    `the debenture, or unit of debenture, is issued by a trustee of a trust on behalf of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debenture, or unit of a debenture, issued by a trustee of a trust on behalf of the trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(4A) the instrument is within the references to a debenture in this Division` MEANS
    IF `the debenture, or unit of debenture, is issued by a trustee of a trust on behalf of the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a debenture includes a debenture, or a unit of debenture, issued by a trustee of a trust on behalf of the trust" lists without closing the list

-- s 239(5): the Authority's written notice imposes conditions on a prescribed entity, who must comply with every one not revoked.
DECLARE `s 239(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 239(5) comply with the condition or restriction`
    `s 239(5) contravene the condition or restriction`

-- src:37779 | (5) The Authority may, by written notice —
-- src:37781 | (a) impose such conditions or restrictions on a prescribed
-- src:37782 | entity as it thinks fit; and
-- src:37787 | (b) at any time vary or revoke any condition or restriction so
-- src:37788 | imposed,
-- src:37790 | and the prescribed entity must comply with every such condition or
-- src:37791 | restriction imposed on it by the Authority that has not been revoked
-- src:37792 | by the Authority.
@ref s 239(5) (the duty to comply) (src:37779-37792)
GIVEN
    `the body is a prescribed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a prescribed entity as section 239(4) defines it?
    `the Authority has imposed the condition or restriction on the prescribed entity by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by written notice, imposed the condition or restriction on the prescribed entity?
    `the Authority has revoked the condition or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked the condition or restriction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(5) the prescribed entity must comply with the condition or restriction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the body is a prescribed entity`) OR (NOT `the Authority has imposed the condition or restriction on the prescribed entity by written notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the prescribed entity must comply with every such condition or restriction imposed on it by the Authority"
        IF `the Authority has revoked the condition or restriction`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that has not been revoked by the Authority"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 239(5A): the offence and its penalty.
-- src:37794 | (5A) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:37795 | imposed under subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:37796 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the
-- src:37797 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000
-- src:37798 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:37799 | conviction.
@ref s 239(5A) (src:37794-37799)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene a condition or restriction imposed under section 239(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F1 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 239(5A) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction imposed under subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 239(5A) (the penalty) (src:37794-37799)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 239(5A) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- The duty as a prohibition-shaped rule: contravening a condition is the failure; no time limit or other consequence is stated here (s 239(5A) makes it an offence).
@ref s 239(5A) (the prohibition on contravening a condition) (src:37794-37799)
GIVEN
    `the prescribed entity` IS A Party @desc Who is the prescribed entity?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 239(5) action`
`s 239(5A) the prescribed entity shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    PARTY `the prescribed entity`
    SHANT `s 239(5) contravene the condition or restriction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the prescribed entity` BECAUSE "a condition or restriction imposed under section 239(5) was contravened, which is an offence under section 239(5A)"

-- s 239(6): when a person makes an offer. "If, and only if" closes the list.
-- src:37801 | (6) For the purposes of this Division, a person makes an offer of any
-- src:37802 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts if, and only if, as
-- src:37803 | principal —
-- src:37805 | (a) the person makes (either personally or by an agent) an offer
-- src:37806 | to any person in Singapore which upon acceptance would
-- src:37807 | give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of those
-- src:37808 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts by the
-- src:37809 | firstmentioned person or another person with whom the
-- src:37810 | firstmentioned person has made arrangements for that
-- src:37811 | issue or sale; or
-- src:37813 | (b) the person invites (either personally or by an agent) any
-- src:37814 | person in Singapore to make an offer which upon
-- src:37815 | acceptance would give rise to a contract for the issue or
-- src:37816 | sale of those securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:37817 | contracts by the firstmentioned person or another person
-- src:37818 | with whom the firstmentioned person has made
-- src:37819 | arrangements for that issue or sale.
@ref s 239(6) (src:37801-37819)
GIVEN
    `the person acts as principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as principal?
    `the person makes an offer, personally or by an agent, to a person in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person make an offer, personally or by an agent, to any person in Singapore?
    `on acceptance the offer would give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by the person or by another person with whom the person has made arrangements for that issue or sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the offer, on acceptance, give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by you, or by another person with whom you have made arrangements for that issue or sale?
    `the person invites, personally or by an agent, a person in Singapore to make an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person invite, personally or by an agent, any person in Singapore to make an offer?
    `the offer the person invites would on acceptance give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by the person or by another person with whom the person has made arrangements for that issue or sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the offer you invite, on acceptance, give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by you, or by another person with whom you have made arrangements for that issue or sale?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(6) the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` MEANS
    IF `the person acts as principal` AND ((`the person makes an offer, personally or by an agent, to a person in Singapore` AND `on acceptance the offer would give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by the person or by another person with whom the person has made arrangements for that issue or sale`) OR (`the person invites, personally or by an agent, a person in Singapore to make an offer` AND `the offer the person invites would on acceptance give rise to a contract for the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts by the person or by another person with whom the person has made arrangements for that issue or sale`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person makes an offer of any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts if, and only if, as principal"

-- s 239(7): "sale" includes any disposal for valuable consideration.
-- src:37823 | (7) In subsection (6), “sale” includes any disposal for valuable
-- src:37824 | consideration.
@ref s 239(7) (src:37823-37824)
GIVEN
    `the disposal is for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disposal made for valuable consideration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(7) the disposal is a sale for the purposes of subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF `the disposal is for valuable consideration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In subsection (6), sale includes any disposal for valuable consideration" lists without closing the list

-- s 239(8): the Division applies only to offers made on or after 1 July 2002.
-- src:37826 | (8) This Division applies only in relation to offers of securities or
-- src:37827 | securities‑based derivatives contracts made on or after 1 July 2002.
@ref s 239(8) (src:37826-37827)
GIVEN
    `the date the offer was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239(8) this Division applies to the offer` MEANS
    IF `the date the offer was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 7 2002)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Division applies only in relation to offers of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made on or after 1 July 2002"

§ `s 239AA: offers of sponsored depositary receipts`

-- inert (reason 1), lines 37834-37835: heading "Offers of sponsored depositary receipts".
-- inert (reason 1), lines 37836-37836: s 239AA(1) chapeau "In this Division": introduces the two definitions below.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 37901-37901: amendment marks.

-- "depositary".
-- src:37838 | “depositary”, in relation to an offer of SDRs, means the issuer of
-- src:37839 | those SDRs that holds, directly or indirectly, the underlying
-- src:37840 | securities;
@ref s 239AA(1) "depositary" (src:37838-37840)
GIVEN
    `the person is the issuer of the SDRs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the issuer of the SDRs offered?
    `the person holds, directly or indirectly, the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold, directly or indirectly, the underlying securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239AA(1) "depositary" the person is the depositary in relation to the offer of SDRs` MEANS
    IF `the person is the issuer of the SDRs` AND `the person holds, directly or indirectly, the underlying securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an offer of SDRs, means the issuer of those SDRs that holds, directly or indirectly, the underlying securities"

-- "SDR" or "sponsored depositary receipt".
-- src:37842 | “SDR” or “sponsored depositary receipt” means an instrument
-- src:37843 | that —
-- src:37845 | (a) confers or represents a right to exchange the
-- src:37846 | instrument for any underlying securities under a
-- src:37847 | trust, contractual arrangement or otherwise;
-- src:37849 | (b) entitles the holder of the instrument to receive —
-- src:37851 | (i) all or substantially all of the interest, dividends
-- src:37852 | or other distributions that are paid or made in
-- src:37853 | relation to the underlying securities; and
-- src:37855 | (ii) any other financial benefits conferred on the
-- src:37856 | holder of the underlying securities, whether in
-- src:37857 | cash or otherwise; and
-- src:37859 | (c) is issued pursuant to an agreement between the
-- src:37860 | depositary that issued the instrument and the issuer of
-- src:37861 | the underlying securities,
-- src:37863 | and that is prescribed, or that belongs to a class of instruments
-- src:37864 | prescribed, by the Authority as an SDR for the purpose of this
-- src:37865 | definition.
@ref s 239AA(1) "SDR" (src:37842-37865)
GIVEN
    `the instrument confers or represents a right to exchange the instrument for any underlying securities under a trust, contractual arrangement or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument confer or represent a right to exchange it for any underlying securities, under a trust, contractual arrangement or otherwise?
    `the instrument entitles the holder to receive all or substantially all of the interest, dividends or other distributions paid or made in relation to the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument entitle the holder to receive all or substantially all of the interest, dividends or other distributions paid or made in relation to the underlying securities?
    `the instrument entitles the holder to receive any other financial benefits conferred on the holder of the underlying securities, whether in cash or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument entitle the holder to receive any other financial benefits conferred on the holder of the underlying securities, in cash or otherwise?
    `the instrument is issued pursuant to an agreement between the depositary that issued it and the issuer of the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument issued under an agreement between the depositary that issued it and the issuer of the underlying securities?
    `the Authority has prescribed the instrument, or its class of instruments, as an SDR for the purpose of this definition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the instrument, or its class of instruments, as an SDR for the purpose of the definition in section 239AA(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239AA(1) "SDR" the instrument is an SDR or sponsored depositary receipt` MEANS
    IF `the instrument confers or represents a right to exchange the instrument for any underlying securities under a trust, contractual arrangement or otherwise` AND `the instrument entitles the holder to receive all or substantially all of the interest, dividends or other distributions paid or made in relation to the underlying securities` AND `the instrument entitles the holder to receive any other financial benefits conferred on the holder of the underlying securities, whether in cash or otherwise` AND `the instrument is issued pursuant to an agreement between the depositary that issued it and the issuer of the underlying securities` AND `the Authority has prescribed the instrument, or its class of instruments, as an SDR for the purpose of this definition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an instrument that (a) confers or represents a right to exchange the instrument for any underlying securities under a trust, contractual arrangement or otherwise; (b) entitles the holder of the instrument to receive (i) all or substantially all of the interest, dividends or other distributions that are paid or made in relation to the underlying securities; and (ii) any other financial benefits conferred on the holder of the underlying securities, whether in cash or otherwise; and (c) is issued pursuant to an agreement between the depositary that issued the instrument and the issuer of the underlying securities, and that is prescribed, or that belongs to a class of instruments prescribed, by the Authority as an SDR for the purpose of this definition"

-- s 239AA(2): an offer of securities includes an offer of SDRs that are securities by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of the definition of "securities" in section 2(1) and not excluded by paragraph (g).
-- The keel's function `s 2(1) "securities" the instrument is securities` answers the paragraph (a), (b), (c) and (g) limbs; the exclusions (d), (e) and (f) are not mentioned by section 239AA(2) and are passed as FALSE (fork F2).
-- src:37867 | (2) In this Division, unless otherwise provided —
-- src:37869 | (a) a reference to an offer of SDRs is a reference to; and
-- src:37871 | (b) a reference to an offer of securities includes a reference to,
-- src:37873 | an offer of SDRs that are securities by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or
-- src:37874 | (c) of the definition of “securities” in section 2(1), and not excluded
-- src:37875 | by virtue of paragraph (g) of that definition.
@ref s 239AA(2) (src:37867-37875)
GIVEN
    `the SDRs are a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the SDRs a share?
    `the SDRs are a unit in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the SDRs a unit in a business trust?
    `the SDRs confer or represent a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the SDRs confer or represent a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership?
    `the SDRs are a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the SDRs a debenture (as section 2(1) defines "debenture")?
    `the Authority has prescribed the SDRs, or their class, as securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the SDRs, or their class of products, as securities?
    `the Authority has prescribed the SDRs, or their class, as not being securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the SDRs, or their class of products, as not being securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F2 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 239AA(2) the offer of SDRs is within the references to an offer of securities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Authority has prescribed the SDRs, or their class, as not being securities`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and not excluded by virtue of paragraph (g) of that definition"
        IF (`s 2(1) "securities" the instrument is securities` `the SDRs are a share` `the SDRs are a unit in a business trust` `the SDRs confer or represent a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership` `the SDRs are a debenture` `the Authority has prescribed the SDRs, or their class, as securities` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to an offer of securities includes a reference to, an offer of SDRs that are securities by virtue of paragraph (a), (b) or (c)" lists without closing the list

-- s 239AA(3): where the depositary (Y) offers SDRs, the issuer of the underlying securities (X) is the issuer and the offeror and has the rights and duties of both.
-- src:37877 | (3) In this Division, where there is an offer of SDRs by the
-- src:37878 | depositary (Y) —
-- src:37883 | (a) the issuer of the underlying securities (X), rather than Y, is
-- src:37884 | treated as the issuer of the SDRs being offered;
@ref s 239AA(3)(a) (src:37877-37884)
GIVEN
    `there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of SDRs by the depositary?
    `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the issuer of the underlying securities?
    `the person is the depositary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the depositary that makes the offer of SDRs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239AA(3)(a) the person is treated as the issuer of the SDRs being offered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary (Y)" is the only case subsection (3) speaks of
        IF `the person is the depositary` AND (NOT `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the issuer of the underlying securities (X), rather than Y, is treated as the issuer of the SDRs being offered"
        IF `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names only X and Y

-- src:37886 | (b) X rather than Y is treated as the person who makes the offer;
-- src:37887 | and
@ref s 239AA(3)(b) (src:37886-37887)
GIVEN
    `there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of SDRs by the depositary?
    `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the issuer of the underlying securities?
    `the person is the depositary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the depositary that makes the offer of SDRs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239AA(3)(b) the person is treated as the person who makes the offer of the SDRs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary (Y)" is the only case subsection (3) speaks of
        IF `the person is the depositary` AND (NOT `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "X rather than Y is treated as the person who makes the offer"
        IF `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names only X and Y

-- src:37889 | (c) accordingly, X has the rights and duties under this Act
-- src:37890 | (including but not limited to compliance with all
-- src:37891 | requirements as to the contents of prospectuses, and
-- src:37892 | liability in respect of statements and non-disclosure in
-- src:37893 | prospectuses) of —
-- src:37895 | (i) the issuer of the SDRs; and
-- src:37897 | (ii) the person making the offer of the SDRs.
@ref s 239AA(3)(c) (src:37889-37897)
GIVEN
    `there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of SDRs by the depositary?
    `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the issuer of the underlying securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239AA(3)(c) the person has the rights and duties under this Act of the issuer and of the person making the offer` MEANS
    IF `there is an offer of SDRs by the depositary` AND `the person is the issuer of the underlying securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "accordingly, X has the rights and duties under this Act" says what X has and does not say that no one else has them

-- s 239AA(4): subsection (3) applies despite s 239(1) "issuer"; the person who is the issuer of an offer of SDRs by the depositary is X.
-- src:37899 | (4) Subsection (3) applies despite anything in section 239.
@ref s 239AA(4) (src:37899-37899)
GIVEN
    `what section 239AA(3)(a) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239AA(3)(a) the person is treated as the issuer of the SDRs being offered` answer for the person?
    `what section 239(1) "issuer" answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239(1) "issuer" the person is the issuer in relation to the offer` answer for the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239AA(4) the person is the issuer of the SDRs, section 239AA(3) prevailing over section 239` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`what section 239AA(3)(a) answers for the person` EQUALS NOTHING))
        THEN `what section 239AA(3)(a) answers for the person`
        OTHERWISE `what section 239(1) "issuer" answers for the person`

§ `s 239A and s 239B: the Authority's power to disapply the Division, and its power to modify`

-- inert (reason 1), lines 37903-37904: heading "Authority may disapply this Division to certain offers".
-- s 239A(1): the Authority's declaration by order in the Gazette that this Division does not apply to the offer or its class.
-- src:37905 | 239A.—(1) Despite any provision to the contrary in this Division,
-- src:37906 | where —
-- src:37908 | (a) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:37909 | contracts is one to which (but for this section) both this
-- src:37910 | Division and Division 2 apply; and
-- src:37912 | (b) the Authority has by order in the Gazette declared that this
-- src:37913 | Division does not apply to that offer or a class of offers to
-- src:37914 | which that offer belongs,
-- src:37916 | then this Division does not apply to that offer.
@ref s 239A(1) (src:37905-37916)
GIVEN
    `the offer is one to which, but for section 239A, both this Division and Division 2 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer one to which both Division 1 and Division 2 of Part 13 would apply, were it not for section 239A?
    `the Authority has by order in the Gazette declared that this Division does not apply to the offer or to a class of offers to which it belongs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by order in the Gazette, declared that Division 1 of Part 13 does not apply to the offer, or to a class of offers to which it belongs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239A(1) the Authority's declaration disapplies this Division to the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is one to which, but for section 239A, both this Division and Division 2 apply` AND `the Authority has by order in the Gazette declared that this Division does not apply to the offer or to a class of offers to which it belongs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where (a) an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is one to which (but for this section) both this Division and Division 2 apply; and (b) the Authority has by order in the Gazette declared that this Division does not apply to that offer or a class of offers to which that offer belongs, then this Division does not apply to that offer"  -- a "where" gate, JUST FALSE under the periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05

-- s 239A(2): units and derivatives of units in a business trust that is also a collective investment scheme.
-- src:37920 | (2) This Division does not apply to an offer of securities or
-- src:37921 | securities‑based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of
-- src:37922 | units in a business trust, where —
-- src:37924 | (a) the business trust is also a collective investment scheme
-- src:37925 | that has been authorised under section 286 or recognised
-- src:37926 | under section 287; or
-- src:37931 | (b) the business trust is also a collective investment scheme
-- src:37932 | and the offer is made in reliance on an exemption under
-- src:37933 | Subdivision (4) of Division 2.
@ref s 239A(2) (src:37920-37933)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units, or derivatives of units, in a business trust?
    `the business trust is also a collective investment scheme authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business trust also a collective investment scheme that has been authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287?
    `the business trust is also a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business trust also a collective investment scheme?
    `the offer is made in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2 of Part 13?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239A(2) this Division does not apply to the offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a business trust` AND (`the business trust is also a collective investment scheme authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287` OR (`the business trust is also a collective investment scheme` AND `the offer is made in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Division does not apply to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a business trust, where (a) the business trust is also a collective investment scheme that has been authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287; or (b) the business trust is also a collective investment scheme and the offer is made in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2"  -- a "where" gate, JUST FALSE under the periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05

-- The four ways the Division (and so Subdivision (2)) can be switched off for an offer, read together:
-- s 239(8) (offers made before 1 July 2002), s 239A(1) and (2) (the Authority's declaration; units in a business trust that is also a scheme)
-- and Subdivision (4) of this Division (sfad's exemptions, which say "Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257) do not apply").
-- The answer of each is passed in as it is (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING), so an answer nobody has worked out stays NOTHING.
-- src:37826 | (8) This Division applies only in relation to offers of securities or
-- src:37827 | securities‑based derivatives contracts made on or after 1 July 2002.
-- src:37905 | 239A.—(1) Despite any provision to the contrary in this Division,
-- src:37906 | where —
-- src:37908 | (a) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:37909 | contracts is one to which (but for this section) both this
-- src:37910 | Division and Division 2 apply; and
-- src:37912 | (b) the Authority has by order in the Gazette declared that this
-- src:37913 | Division does not apply to that offer or a class of offers to
-- src:37914 | which that offer belongs,
-- src:37916 | then this Division does not apply to that offer.
@ref s 239(8) and s 239A(1) read with Subdivision (4) of Division 1 (src:37826-37916)
GIVEN
    `what section 239(8) answers for the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239(8) this Division applies to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 239A(1) answers for the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(1) the Authority's declaration disapplies this Division to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 239A(2) answers for the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(2) this Division does not apply to the offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the offer is exempted from Subdivision (2) by a provision of Subdivision (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13 (sections 272 to 282) say that Subdivision (2) of that Division does not apply to the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 239A(1) answers for the offer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 239A(2) answers for the offer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the offer is exempted from Subdivision (2) by a provision of Subdivision (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then this Division does not apply to that offer"; "This Division does not apply to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a business trust"; "Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257) do not apply to an offer"
        IF `what section 239(8) answers for the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
